course: dictionary
lesson: 15322
title: Snare: a trap, a trick, or a drum
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A snare is a trap for catching animals, usually a loop of wire or string that tightens around the animal. Hunters and poachers set snares for rabbits and birds. «The rabbit was caught in a snare set by the hedge.» The word caught tells you the trap worked.
explain: Snare can also mean something that tricks a person. «The clever questions were a snare, and he fell right into them.» Here there is no wire at all. The snare is a trick made of words. Look at the clues around the word: fell into them tells you the trick worked.
explain: Snare is also a music word. A snare drum is a small drum with wires underneath that make a sharp rattle. «The snare cracked loudly as the band marched past.» Drums and band are in the sentence, so you can guess it is music.
explain: As a verb, snare means to catch. «She snared the last ticket before they sold out.» Test your meaning by swapping it in: "She caught the last ticket before they sold out." It still makes sense, so snared means caught or won, here by skill or luck.
fact: A snare is a trap for animals, usually a loop of wire or string that tightens.
fact: «Snare» can also mean a trick that catches a person, like a trap made of words.
fact: A snare drum is a small drum with wires underneath that give a sharp rattle.
fact: As a verb, «snare» means to catch an animal in a trap, or to catch or win something by skill or a trick.
fact: Useful phrases include «set a snare», «caught in a snare» and «snare drum».
exercise: «The fox was caught in a snare set by the farmer.» What is a snare here? | A small drum with wires underneath | *A trap for catching animals | A loud shout across the field | A soft blanket for the cold
exercise: «The clever questions were a snare, and he fell right into them.» What does snare mean here? | A large, soft bed | *A trick that catches a person | A drum for the marching band | A loop of wire for catching birds
exercise: The band played and Ella heard the snare crack loudly. What is a snare in a band? | *A small drum with wires underneath | A tall tree in the forest | A loop of string for catching rabbits | A kind of wooden door
test: «She snared the last ticket before they sold out.» What does snared mean? | *Caught or won by skill or a trick | Lost in the rain | Washed clean in the river | Torn into small pieces
test: In «The snare sounded sharp in the band», what is a snare? | *A snare drum with wires underneath | A trick made of words | A lost ticket on the ground | A loop of wire for catching foxes
exam: Which sentence uses snare as a verb, meaning to catch? | The snare was made of wire | *The hunter will snare the rabbit before dark | The clever snare fooled the crowd | The snare drum rattled loudly
